---
description: Avoid optional props/args by default; model absence explicitly in types
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript: avoid optional properties & arguments

- **No optional properties by default**: Prefer required fields. If something can be missing, model it explicitly via unions.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
type Config = { apiKey?: string };

// ✅ GOOD (field always present, but value may be undefined)
type Config = { apiKey: string | undefined };

// ✅ GOOD (mutually exclusive shapes / discriminated union)
type Config = { apiKey: string } | { apiKey: undefined; reason: 'missing' };
```

- **No optional arguments by default**: Prefer an options object with required keys, overloads, or separate functions.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function connect(url?: string) {}

// ✅ GOOD
function connect(options: { url: string }) {}
```
